          "The parent re-renders for any reason",
          "A context value changes"
        ],
        "answer": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "q2",
        "text": "Passing an inline object as a prop causes a re-render because:",
        "options": [
          "Objects are expensive to create",
          "A new reference is created on every render",
          "React deep-compares props",
          "It breaks the rules of hooks"
        ],
        "answer": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "q3",
        "text": "Before optimising, you should:",
        "options": [
          "Wrap everything in useMemo",
          "Profile and find the actual cost",
          "Split every component",
          "Disable StrictMode"
        ],
        "answer": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "q4",
        "text": "List virtualisation helps because it:",
        "options": [
          "Renders only the visible rows",
          "Compresses the data",
          "Removes keys from the list",
          "Moves rendering to a worker"
        ],
        "answer": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "q5",
        "text": "An unstable context value is a problem because:",
        "options": [
          "It throws in development",
          "Every consumer re-renders whenever the provider renders",
          "It disables Suspense",
          "It prevents code splitting"
        ],
        "answer": 1
      }
    ]
